-- Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two, four power armors (printed 61-72): Aurora Blazer, Beach-Stormer, Blue Boy, Blue Hawk
-- 4 vehicle rows, with 41 locations and 9 weapon entries.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/~299-northern-gun-2-power-armor-a.sql
--
-- Written by scripts/vessel-sql.mjs from 1 worker file(s). Every value
-- is printable ASCII, every row cites its book, and a Main Body location
-- agrees with its vehicle's mdc_main_body.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, is_mega_damage, ar, cost, cost_note, description, source_book) VALUES
  ('ng-x30-aurora-blazer', 'Aurora Blazer Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 90 mph (144 km) top speed, tiring the pilot at 25% of the normal rate (10% at 50 mph/80 km or less). Power jumping travel: 175 mph (280 km), sustainable for hours; reduce by 40% in dense brush, deep mud or snow, rocky ground and similar terrain. Leaping: 15 ft (4.6 m) up or across unassisted, 25 ft (7.6 m) with only the leg jets (+50% with a running start for either), and up to 200 ft (61 m) high and 300 ft (91.4 m) across with full thrust. VTOL leap: straight up 300 ft (91.4 m), then hover 1D4+1 melee rounds.', 'Limited flight: 100 mph (160 km) maximum, cruising about 60 mph (96 km); maximum altitude 200 ft (61 m), flight wobbly. Loses 20 ft (6.1 m) of altitude every 10 minutes and must land and take off again; one hour of this, then the back thrusters need 60 minutes to cool.', 'Swims 15 mph (24 km/13 knots) on the surface or submerged without the jets (20% fatigue rate); 35 mph (56 km/30 knots) underwater on the jet thrusters; walks the bottom at 15 mph (24 km). Maximum depth 1,200 ft (366 m).', 'Height 7 ft 2 in (2.2 m); width 4 ft (1.2 m); length 3.5 ft (1.1 m)', 'Roughly 540 lbs (243 kg)', 175, 1, NULL, 1100000, '2.8 million credits nuclear, 1.6 million Solid Oxide, 1.1 million electric battery; the lowest is stored.', 'Model Type: NG-X30. Class: All-Terrain Recon and High Speed Assault Power Armor. One of Northern Gun''s newest suits: a light, fast leaper in the spirit of the Triax Terrain Hopper, with two rotating back thrusters and jets in the lower legs that let it bound, hover briefly and land vertically. Rumour links its SAMAS-like layout to a secret NG flight-armor program. Favoured for scouting, escort, rescue, hit-and-run raids and naval work: it can dive, approach a ship underwater and rocket onto its deck, or attack hulls, submarines and sea monsters from below. Cat-like landings: falls of up to 500 ft (152 m) are cushioned by the thrusters; from 500 to 900 ft (152-274 m) roll 1D20, and on 1-10 the suit takes 4D6 M.D. and the pilot loses 1D4 melee actions; anything higher does 2D4x10 M.D. to the suit, 6D6 S.D.C./Hit Points to the pilot and stuns him 1D4 melee rounds. Power jumping is loud and costs -3 on initiative and Perception and -1 to strike, parry and dodge. Bonuses: +1 to dodge, +2 to dodge above 90 mph (144 km), +1 to roll with impact. Robot P.S. 28. Cargo: none. Power: nuclear, 12 year average life; Solid Oxide and electric battery versions are sold too. Comes standard with NG''s Universal Energy Link (UEL): an E-Clip-shaped connector on a cable from the suit''s power supply that gives any E-Clip energy weapon of 1D6x10 M.D. or less per blast an unlimited payload (a stronger weapon trips a breaker and will not fire; no effect on projectile weapons). It fits most North American makers'' guns, most Triax, Japanese and Chinese ones, and about a third of Naruni''s. The cable takes 5 M.D.C. to cut and needs a Called Shot at -6 (-10 while the suit moves or dodges). The weapon text places the three UELs in each forearm and the right shoulder; the introduction says the right shoulder and the left forearm. Any handheld weapon may be used, with a sidearm, Vibro-Blade and gear on a belt. Hand to hand per Basic or Elite Flying Power Armor Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.351-352): restrained punch 1D4 M.D., full punch 1D6, power punch 2D6 (two attacks), power dive punch 3D6 (two attacks, bonuses other than strike halved), kick 2D4, leap kick 2D8 (two attacks), high-speed running or rocketing leap kick 3D8+3 (two attacks). Sensors beyond the NG standard: helmet and concealed gun cameras (96 hours of video, 4,000 stills), two cheek LED lamps (500 ft/152 m) and a language translator. The M.D.C. list includes a booster pack and rail gun ammo canister on the back, though no rail gun is among the weapon systems.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.61-65'),
  ('ng-nx12-beach-stormer', 'Beach-Stormer Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 40 mph (64 km) maximum, +10 mph (16 km) with the hydro-jet pack removed; 10% of the normal fatigue rate. Leaping: 15 ft (4.6 m) high or 25 ft (7.6 m) across.', 'Not possible.', 'Hydro-jet pack: 35 mph (56 km/30 knots) on the surface, 20 mph (32 km/17 knots) submerged. Without it: swims 10 mph (16 km/8.6 knots) or walks the sea floor at 4 mph (6.4 km). Maximum depth 3,000 ft (914 m).', 'Height 7.2 ft (2.2 m); width 4 ft (1.2 m); length 5 ft (1.5 m) with the hydro-jet pack, 3 ft 4 in (1 m) without', '326 lbs (146.7 kg) total; 280 lbs (126 kg) without weapons', 170, 1, NULL, 340000, '340,000 credits for the original electric battery model, complete with the NG-P67 Short-Gun, the NG-M100 rifle, 10 extra E-Clips and a load of grenades or torpedoes; 720,000 with a Solid Oxide power system; 1.2 million nuclear. The lowest is stored.', 'Model Type: NG-NX12. Class: Amphibious Infantry Assault Suit. Northern Gun''s first marine power armor, built because no North American maker offered marine infantry anything better than body armor. A cheap, tough suit with a detachable hydro-jet pack, quick in the water, used for scouting, underwater demolition, sabotage, rescue, ship escort, beach reconnaissance, boarding actions and amphibious landings. Robot P.S. 24. Cargo: none. Power: a rechargeable battery good for 96 hours of continuous use (4-12 days of normal service), recharged in about 2 hours from any vehicle or facility with a generator; Solid Oxide and nuclear (15 year life) versions are sold as well. Otherwise it has every standard NG power armor system. Range is unlimited when nuclear powered. Hand to hand per Basic or Elite Ground-Based Power Armor Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.351-352): restrained punch 1D4 M.D., full punch 1D4, power punch 2D4 (two attacks), power dive punch 2D6 (two attacks, bonuses other than strike halved), kick 1D6, leap kick 2D6 (two attacks). Both standard weapons are sold separately as gear.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.65-67'),
  ('ng-x44-blue-boy', 'Blue Boy Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 40 mph (64 km) maximum, 20% of the normal fatigue rate. Leaping: 10 ft (3 m) high or 16 ft (4.9 m) across. Climbing: +5% to Climb skill, +10% with the magnets on metal; speed halved while walking on the magnetic plates.', 'None, unless fitted with a jet pack or a Silent Shadow style glider (either costs extra).', 'Not built for water; swims or walks the bottom at 5 mph (8 km/4.3 knots), 20% fatigue rate. Maximum depth 800 ft (244 m).', 'Man-size: height generally 5.6 to 7.6 ft (1.7 to 2.3 m); width 2-3 ft (0.6 to 0.9 m); length 2.5 to 3 ft (0.75 to 0.9 m)', '326 lbs (146.7 kg)', 165, 1, NULL, 832000, '1.2 million credits nuclear or 832,000 Solid Oxide; the lowest is stored. Nuclear outsells Solid Oxide five to one.', 'Model Type: NG-X44. Class: Light Infantry Assault and Saboteur Power Armor. Northern Gun''s answer to the Coalition Dead Boy: a sleek, man-sized, heavily armored infantry suit that ships in a metallic blue (the suit on the cover of Northern Gun One). Fit for combat, support, scouting and adventuring, with features aimed at special operations and sabotage: a small profile, magnetic plates in the feet and palms for clinging to and riding robots and vehicles or scaling ship hulls and metal towers, an electrical dart weapon for knocking out electronics or stunning prisoners, and the exclusive Thumper shoulder gun. Its blended metal, ceramic and plastic M.D.C. alloy is light and shrugs off electricity and EMP: half damage, with no risk to its electronics or memory. Robot P.S. 25. Cargo: none. Power: nuclear standard, 10 year average life; Solid Oxide sold too. Any other handheld weapon (sidearm, Vibro-Blade, shotgun) can ride on a belt or two or in a bag. Hand to hand per Ground-Based Power Armor Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.352): restrained punch printed as 6D6 M.D. (more than the normal punch, so likely a misprint), normal punch 1D4 M.D., power punch 2D4 (two attacks), kick 1D6, leap kick 2D6 (two attacks). The M.D.C. list includes two Vibro-Blades (15 each) that the weapon systems do not describe. Sensors beyond the NG standard: a language translator (nine languages of the Americas plus room for 12; 98.7% accurate with a three second delay for one speaker, 78% and six seconds for three), passive nightvision (2,000 ft/610 m), a telescopic helmet camera (2 miles/3.2 km), and the EMP-resistant alloy and magnetic climbing system above.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.67-69'),
  ('ng-ax19-blue-hawk', 'Blue Hawk Flying Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 60 mph (96 km) maximum, 20% of the normal fatigue rate. Leaping: 15 ft (4.6 m) high or across unassisted; jet-assisted up to 100 ft (30.5 m) high and 200 ft (61 m) across, or a dive 200 ft (61 m) into water in 4 seconds.', 'Hovers up to 400 ft (122 m); maximum 290 mph (464 km), cruising 100-150 mph (160-240 km); maximum altitude 2,000 ft (610 m). The jets need to cool after at most eight hours of continuous flight; rests every 2-5 hours allow indefinite flight.', 'About 40 mph (64 km/34 knots) with the aquatic propulsion system, or walks the bottom at 5 mph (8 km). Maximum depth 3,000 ft (914 m).', 'Height about 8 ft (2.4 m), 9 ft (2.7 m) to the top of the propulsion system; width 4 ft (1.2 m) wings folded, 14 ft (4.3 m) extended; length 4 ft 9 in (1.45 m)', '594 lbs (267 kg)', 200, 1, NULL, 950000, '1.9 million credits nuclear, 1.4 million Solid Oxide, 950,000 electric battery; the lowest is stored. Good to excellent availability at Ishpeming/Upper Michigan, fair at MercTown, poor elsewhere.', 'Model Type: NG-AX19 (the section heading on p.69 calls it the NG-AX15). Class: Armored Flying Infantry Assault Suit. Also called the Sea Hawk: the air-and-water sibling of the Red Hawk, which works alongside it, with an underwater propulsion system where the Red Hawk carries its super-thruster. Built for the Great Lakes and the sea: escorting ships, coastal patrol, hunting pirates and sea serpents, rescue on the water, and increasingly fighting Xiticix in Wisconsin and Michigan, escaping them by diving (the bugs give up after 1D6+6 minutes). It can drop a sonar pod on a 25 ft (7.6 m) cable while hovering to search a 50 mile (80 km) diameter, then fly or swim to the contact. Firing from the air into the water is -2 to strike, and Great Lakes targets deeper than 120 ft (36.6 m) are usually invisible from above. Losing a wing ends flight, though jet-assisted leaps remain. Robot P.S. 28 (the hand to hand section bases damage on 26). Cargo: none. Power: nuclear, 12 year average life (flying range text gives 15 years); Solid Oxide and electric battery models also exist. Two UELs, one under the plating of each forearm, power any E-Clip energy weapon of 1D6x10 M.D. or less with an unlimited payload; any other handheld weapon may be used, with a sidearm, Vibro-Blade and spare grenades on one or two belts. Hand to hand per Basic or Elite Flying Power Armor Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.351-352): restrained punch 1D4 M.D., full punch 1D6, power punch 2D6 (two attacks), power dive punch 3D6 (two attacks, bonuses other than strike halved), kick 2D4, leap kick 2D8 (two attacks). Sensors beyond the NG standard: three belly infrared searchlights (1,000 ft/305 m), enhanced radar tracking 96 targets at 100 miles (160 km) while airborne, enhanced sonar tracking 96 targets in a 50 mile (80 km) diameter underwater plus the lowered probe (readings after 1D4 melee rounds, hovering or under 20 mph/32 km), a language translator, nightvision (2,000 ft/610 m) with infrared and ultraviolet optics (1,000 ft/305 m), and telescopic and macro cameras in the rifle, chest and eyes (2 miles/3.2 km, 12x; 100 hours of video, 4,000 stills).', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.69-72');

